<HelpChapterSection Id="admin">
    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-overview">
        <p>The <span class="help-ui">Administration</span> menu item is visible to users with at least one administrative permission. The page contains tiles, each shown only if you have the matching permission:</p>
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Tile</th><th>What it contains</th><th>Required permission</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Users</td><td>Accounts, positions, blocking, password and 2FA resets.</td><td>View users</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Import and export</td><td>Bulk adding of users from XLSX/CSV and exporting them.</td><td>Import users or Export users</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Roles and permissions</td><td>Permission sets for positions and modules.</td><td>Manage roles</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Structure</td><td>Organizations and their units: departments, divisions, branches (see “<a href="/help#structure-manage">Managing organizations and units</a>”).</td><td>Manage structure</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Unit types</td><td>Names of the structure levels: organization, department, division, section… (see “<a href="/help#structure-types">Unit types</a>”).</td><td>Manage structure</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>News</td><td>Posts and announcements (see “<a href="/help#news-list">Managing posts</a>”).</td><td>Manage news</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Audit log</td><td>Sign-ins, permission changes, document signing.</td><td>Audit log</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p>You manage users, structure and news only in the organizations of your positions — see “<a href="/help#admin-scope">Administration within organizations</a>”.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-scope">
        <p>Several organizations can work in one cabinet, and each administers its own people, structure and news. That is why the permissions “View users”, “Manage users”, “Import users”, “Export users”, “Account security”, “Manage structure” and “Manage news” apply <strong>only in the organizations of your positions</strong> — including all their units and nested (subsidiary) organizations.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>A permission applies in the organization of the position whose role grants it. For example, an HR specialist of organization A who also holds a regular staff position in organization B manages accounts only in A. A permission granted individually applies in the organizations of all your positions.</li>
            <li>The <strong>“Administer all organizations”</strong> permission extends your administrative permissions to the whole cabinet. By default only the “System administrator” role has it; grant it only to administrators of the entire cabinet.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Organization administrator</th><th>Administrator of all organizations</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>User list, user card, export</td><td>Accounts that have at least one position in their organizations. The export includes only positions in these organizations.</td><td>All accounts, including those without positions.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Positions</td><td>Assigns and changes positions only in units of their own organizations.</td><td>In any unit.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Personal details, email, blocking, password, 2FA, sessions, individual permissions</td><td>Only for accounts whose positions are all in their organizations.</td><td>For all accounts (subject to the “<a href="/help#admin-hierarchy">authority limits</a>”).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Import</td><td>Unit codes of their own organizations only; updates only accounts whose positions are all in their organizations; a new account must have a position.</td><td>Without these restrictions.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Structure</td><td>Creates, edits and moves units and subsidiary organizations within their own organizations.</td><td>Also creates and moves top-level organizations, turns an organization into a regular unit and maintains the unit type catalog.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>News</td><td>Publishes and edits news of their own organizations.</td><td>Also news of the whole cabinet and of any organization.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <h4>Account in several organizations</h4>
        <p>If a person holds positions both in your organization and in another one, you see them in the list, and their card is marked “Account in several organizations”. You change only their positions in your organizations; positions in other organizations are shown as “Position in another organization” and cannot be edited, and if the primary position is there, it stays primary. The personal details, email, status and security of such an account are changed by an administrator who manages all of its organizations, or by an administrator of all organizations. Otherwise you will see: “The user also holds positions in organizations you don't manage…”</p>
        <p>An account without any position belongs to no organization, so only an administrator of all organizations can see it. An organization administrator cannot leave a user without positions: “Assign at least one position in a unit of your organization…” — to revoke access, block the account instead.</p>
        <p>Roles, the unit type catalog and the audit log are shared by the whole cabinet: the “Audit log” permission opens events of all organizations.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-users-list">
        <p><span class="help-ui">Administration</span> → <span class="help-ui">Users</span>. Self-registration is disabled — all accounts are created here or by import. The list shows the accounts of your organizations (an administrator of all organizations sees the whole cabinet).</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Search by full name or email; filters: status (<span class="help-ui">All</span> / <span class="help-ui">Active</span> / <span class="help-ui">Blocked</span>), <span class="help-ui">All units</span> (the selected unit together with all nested ones; select an organization to see all of its people), <span class="help-ui">All roles</span>.</li>
            <li>Columns: <strong>User</strong> (full name and email), <strong>Position</strong> (primary position and unit; for people in several organizations — the position in your organization), <strong>Status</strong>, <strong>Last sign-in</strong>, <span class="help-ui">Open</span>.</li>
            <li>Statuses: “Active”, “Blocked” (by an administrator), “Temporarily locked” (after failed sign-in attempts), and also “No 2FA” — the user hasn't set up an authenticator yet.</li>
            <li>Buttons: <span class="help-ui">XLSX</span> / <span class="help-ui">CSV</span> — export the list with the current filters; <span class="help-ui">Import</span>; <span class="help-ui">Add</span> — a new account.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Without the “Manage users” permission, the user card opens read-only.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-users-create">
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Add</span>.</li>
            <li>Fill in “Personal details”: <span class="help-ui">Last name</span>, <span class="help-ui">First name</span> (required), <span class="help-ui">Middle name</span>, <span class="help-ui">Phone</span>, <span class="help-ui">Email (sign-in)</span> (required, unique).</li>
            <li>Add at least one position (see “<a href="/help#admin-users-edit">Personal details and positions</a>”) — without a position the user won't have access to the modules.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Create account</span> — “Account created.”</li>
            <li>A “Temporary password for … (shown once)” block appears. Click <span class="help-ui">Copy</span> — the sign-in email and password are copied.</li>
            <li>Pass the details to the user over a secure channel (in person, by phone, in an end-to-end encrypted messenger — not in group chats and not in the same email as the sign-in name). On first sign-in the user replaces the password with their own and sets up an authenticator.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Possible errors: “A user with this email already exists.”, “Enter a valid email address.”, “Select a unit and a role for each position.”, “You can assign positions only in units of organizations you manage.”, “Assign at least one position in a unit of your organization…”</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-users-edit">
        <p>Open the user (<span class="help-ui">Open</span> in the list). At the top are the full name, email and badges: “Active” / “Blocked”, “2FA enabled” / “2FA not set up”, “Temporary password”, “Sessions: N”.</p>
        <h4>Positions</h4>
        <p>The role of a position defines permissions; the unit defines the scope of access to documents.</p>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Add position</span>.</li>
            <li>Select a <span class="help-ui">Unit</span> and a <span class="help-ui">Role</span>, and enter the <span class="help-ui">Position title</span> (for example, “Chief accountant”; up to 128 characters). The unit list contains only units of organizations you manage; positions in other organizations are assigned by their administrators (see “<a href="/help#admin-scope">Administration within organizations</a>”).</li>
            <li>Check <span class="help-ui">Primary</span> for the main position (only one; if none is selected, the first one becomes primary). The primary position is shown in lists and signing routes; the others count as secondary positions.</li>
            <li>Remove an unneeded position with <span class="help-ui">Remove position</span>. The same “unit + role” pair cannot appear twice.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Save changes</span> — “Changes saved.” The new permissions take effect for the user within a minute.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Without the “Manage roles” permission you can assign only roles whose permissions you all have yourself; the system administrator role is unavailable. Error: “You can't assign the role “X” because it grants more permissions than you have.”</p>
        <p>An account cannot be deleted — only blocked. This preserves the history of documents and signatures.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-users-overrides">
        <p>The “Individual permissions” card (visible with the “Manage roles” permission) lets you grant or deny specific permissions on top of the position roles. For each permission choose:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><span class="help-ui">By roles</span> — as defined by the position roles (default);</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Grant</span> — the permission applies even if the roles don't give it;</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Deny</span> — the permission doesn't apply even if a role gives it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The “in effect” badge marks the permissions the user actually has. Denials don't apply to system administrators. Use individual permissions for exceptions; for typical cases, configure a role instead.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-users-security">
        <p>The “Account security” card on the user's page. Each action requires confirmation.</p>
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Button</th><th>Required permission</th><th>What happens</th><th>When to use</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Block</td><td>Manage users</td><td>Sign-in becomes impossible, all sessions end immediately. “Account blocked.”</td><td>Dismissal, long absence, suspected compromise.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Unblock</td><td>Manage users</td><td>Sign-in is allowed again. “Account unblocked.”</td><td>The employee returns.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Issue a temporary password</td><td>Account security</td><td>The current password stops working, sessions end, a new temporary password is shown (once). “Temporary password issued.”</td><td>The user forgot their password.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Reset authenticator</td><td>Account security</td><td>2FA is turned off, recovery codes are revoked, sessions end. On next sign-in the user sets up a new phone. “Authenticator reset.”</td><td>The user changed or lost their phone.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>End all sessions</td><td>Account security</td><td>All of the user's sessions end; the temporary lockout after failed sign-in attempts is also lifted. “Sessions ended.”</td><td>The user forgot to sign out on someone else's device; the account needs unlocking after failed sign-ins.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p>Before resetting a password or an authenticator, make sure the request really comes from the account owner (in person or via a known phone number). Below the card are the “Created” and “Last sign-in” dates. You cannot block your own account.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-import">
        <p><span class="help-ui">Administration</span> → <span class="help-ui">Import and export</span> (or <span class="help-ui">Import</span> in the user list). Import creates new accounts and updates existing ones (matched by email).</p>
        <h4>Preparing the file</h4>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>In the “Template” card, download the <span class="help-ui">XLSX</span> or <span class="help-ui">CSV</span> template — it contains three examples. Expand <span class="help-ui">Role codes</span> to see the allowed codes.</li>
            <li>Fill in the columns (the first row holds the headers; keep the Ukrainian header names from the template, case doesn't matter):</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Column</th><th>Required</th><th>What to enter</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Email</td><td>yes</td><td>The user's sign-in name. The headers “e-mail”, “пошта” and “електронна пошта” are also accepted.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Прізвище</td><td>yes</td><td>Last name.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Ім'я</td><td>yes</td><td>First name.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>По батькові</td><td>no</td><td>Middle name.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Телефон</td><td>no</td><td>Phone number in the +380… format; an empty cell doesn't erase an existing number.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Код підрозділу</td><td>for a position</td><td>Unit code from the structure (for example, SALES). Codes are unique across all organizations.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Код ролі</td><td>for a position</td><td>Role code (for example, head-of-unit).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Посада</td><td>no</td><td>Position title (for example, “Associate professor”).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Статус</td><td>no</td><td>“заблокований”, “заблоковано”, “blocked”, “inactive”, “0”, “ні” or “no” — the account will be blocked; anything else or empty — active.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <ul>
            <li>Several rows with the same email are several positions of one person. The first row sets the primary position.</li>
            <li>If the file has no positions for an existing user, their positions don't change.</li>
            <li>CSV must be UTF-8 encoded; the delimiter is detected automatically. For XLSX, the first sheet is read.</li>
            <li>Limits: up to 5 MB and up to 10,000 rows.</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>Validation and import</h4>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Drag the file into the “1. Select a file” card and click <span class="help-ui">Validate</span> — the file is checked without saving anything.</li>
            <li>The “2. Validation result” card shows “Rows in file”, “Will be created”, “Will be updated”. If there are errors, a “Row / Email / Error” table appears. Fix the file and validate again: import is possible only when there are no errors.</li>
            <li>When there are no errors, click <span class="help-ui">Import</span>. The import is applied completely or not at all.</li>
            <li>If new accounts were created, the <span class="help-ui">Passwords (XLSX)</span> and <span class="help-ui">Passwords (CSV)</span> buttons appear — a file with the columns “Email”, “Full name”, “Temporary password”. <strong>Download it right away</strong>: passwords are shown only once. Keep the file secure and delete it after handing out the passwords.</li>
        </ol>
        <h4>Common row errors</h4>
        <ul>
            <li>“Invalid email.”, “Last name and first name are required.”</li>
            <li>“Unit with code “X” not found.”, “Role with code “X” not found.”</li>
            <li>“Unit “X” belongs to an organization you don't manage…” — import assigns positions only in your organizations.</li>
            <li>“An account with this email already exists and has positions in organizations you don't manage…” — such an account is changed by an administrator of all of its organizations.</li>
            <li>“Specify the unit code and the role code…” — a new account without a position would end up outside your organizations.</li>
            <li>“You can't assign the role “X”.” — the role grants more permissions than you have.</li>
            <li>“This account has more permissions than you, so the import can't change it.”</li>
            <li>“You can't block your own account.”</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Blocking through import immediately ends the sessions of the blocked users.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-export">
        <ul>
            <li>In the user list, the <span class="help-ui">XLSX</span> / <span class="help-ui">CSV</span> buttons export users <strong>with the current filters applied</strong> (search, status, unit, role).</li>
            <li>The “Export” card on the import page exports <strong>all</strong> users of your organizations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Only positions in your organizations are exported — so the export can be imported back without errors about other organizations' units.</p>
        <p>The format matches the import (the same 9 columns, each position on a separate row, status “активний” / “заблокований”); passwords are not exported. So you can edit the export and import it back for bulk changes. The file name is <code class="ds-code">users-YYYYMMDD-HHMM.xlsx</code> or <code class="ds-code">.csv</code> (CSV uses the “;” delimiter and opens in Excel without any setup).</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-roles">
        <p><span class="help-ui">Administration</span> → <span class="help-ui">Roles and permissions</span>. A role is a set of permissions for a position; a user receives the permissions of all their positions.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>List: search by name or code, columns “Role”, “Code”, “Type” (“System” / “Custom”, and also “Managerial”), “Permissions” (count), “Users” (count), <span class="help-ui">Configure</span>.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">New role</span> — create a custom role for the needs of your field (for example, “Project manager”, “Dean”, “Chief physician”).</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>Configuring a role</h4>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>In the “Role” card, enter the <span class="help-ui">Code</span> (only when creating: lowercase Latin letters, digits and “-”, up to 64 characters, for example <code class="ds-code">project-manager</code> — used in import), the <span class="help-ui">Name</span> (required) and the <span class="help-ui">Description</span>. The <span class="help-ui">Managerial position</span> checkbox lists holders of the role first among the unit's staff, with the “Head” badge.</li>
            <li>In the “Permissions” card, check the permissions you need — they are grouped by module, each with a description.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Save</span> — “Role saved”. The changes take effect for all holders of the role within a minute.</li>
        </ol>
        <ul>
            <li>The names, descriptions and permissions of system roles can be changed (for example, rename “Head of organization” to “Rector” or “CEO”), but the system roles themselves can't be deleted. The “System administrator” role always has all permissions.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Delete role</span> — only for custom roles that aren't assigned to anyone (otherwise: “The role is assigned to users — change their positions first.”).</li>
        </ul>
        <Alert Tone="Tone.Outline" Icon="triangle-alert" Title="Be careful with the “Manage roles” and “Administer all organizations” permissions">Anyone with “Manage roles” can change the permissions of roles and assign any role, including system administrator. “Administer all organizations” extends administrative permissions to the whole cabinet. Grant these permissions only to administrators of the entire cabinet.</Alert>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-audit">
        <p><span class="help-ui">Administration</span> → <span class="help-ui">Audit log</span> — a timeline of important events: who did what, when, and from which IP address.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Search by user name, details or IP.</li>
            <li>Category filter: <span class="help-ui">All events</span>, “Authentication”, “Documents”, “Users”, “Roles”, “Structure”, “News”.</li>
            <li>Period: <span class="help-ui">From date</span> and <span class="help-ui">To date</span> (inclusive). Dates are calendar days in Kyiv time, as are the event times in the table: “to 25.10” covers events up to 23:59 on October 25, Kyiv time.</li>
            <li>Columns “Time” (newest first), “Event” (with details), “User”, “IP”. 50 entries per page.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Events</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Authentication</td><td>Sign-in (with details: “Password + authenticator”, “Password + recovery code”), Failed sign-in attempt, Lockout after sign-in attempts, Sign-out, Authenticator connected, Authenticator reset, New recovery codes, Password change, Password reset, Sessions ended.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Users</td><td>User created, User changed, User status change, User import, User export.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Roles</td><td>Role change, Role deletion.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Structure</td><td>Structure change.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Documents</td><td>Document created, Document changed (with the new file name and the number of revoked signatures), Document sent for signing, Document withdrawn, Document signed (with the format, provider and certificate number), Signing declined, Document archived, Document deleted.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>News</td><td>News change, News deletion.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p>A series of “Failed sign-in attempt” events for one account from different IP addresses may indicate password guessing — check whether the user has 2FA enabled and, if needed, issue a new temporary password.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="admin-hierarchy">
        <p>To prevent any administrator from expanding their own permissions, the following rules apply:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Administrative permissions apply only in the organizations of your positions (see “<a href="/help#admin-scope">Administration within organizations</a>”).</li>
            <li>You can manage only accounts whose permissions you all have too. Otherwise: “This account has more permissions than you, so you can't manage it.” The same rule applies to import.</li>
            <li>Without the “Manage roles” permission you can't assign a role that grants more permissions than you have, nor the system administrator role.</li>
            <li>Individual permissions can be changed only by holders of the “Manage roles” permission.</li>
            <li>You can't block your own account.</li>
            <li>Every administrative action is recorded in the audit log.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpTopicSection>
</HelpChapterSection>
